        <item>
            <key> <string>description</string> </key>
            <value> <string>Download a file or generate a print (PDF/ODT) from an ERP5 document.\n
\n
    Handles the dialog submission pattern: fetches the dialog form, collects defaults,\n
    applies overrides, and submits to download the binary file.\n
\n
    USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - You need to download an attached file (spreadsheet, PDF, image).\n
    - You need to generate a print output (offer PDF, invoice PDF).\n
    - You found download/print actions via erp5_read\'s \'exchanges\' or \'prints\' arrays.\n
\n
    DO NOT USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - You want to read document fields — use erp5_read instead.\n
    - You want to read the text content of a document — use erp5_read (text fields are in fields).\n
\n
    PREREQUISITE: Call erp5_read first — use action names from the \'exchanges\' array\n
    (e.g. \'download\', \'download_ooo\') or \'prints\' array (e.g. \'offer_print\').\n
\n
    REPORTS: an action from erp5_read\'s \'reports\' array works here too and gives\n
    you the report as a rendered file. When you want its numbers as rows you can\n
    read, filter or total instead, use erp5_collect with the report name as\n
    \'view\' - it returns the same report as JSON rows. Come back here for the\n
    PDF/ODS/XLSX, or when erp5_collect reports that a particular report renders\n
    no single table (most accounting reports are built from several sections).\n
</string> </value>
